Use `@variant` to define dark mode styles when `.dark` is applied to `<html>`:

```css
@theme {
  --color-bg-light: oklch(98% 0.002 247);
  --color-text-dark: oklch(20% 0.006 285);
}

@variant dark {
  :root.dark {
    --color-bg-light: oklch(20% 0.006 285);
    --color-text-dark: oklch(98% 0.002 247);
  }
}
```

Then in your HTML:
```html
<html class="dark">
```

You can now use `bg-light` and `text-dark` which will adapt based on the dark class.

